solution:
Since each denominator divides \(1000\), we can express every fraction in thousandths. This makes the fractional units the same size, so we can add their numerators:
\[
\begin{aligned}
\frac{2}{10}+\frac{4}{100}+\frac{6}{1000}
&=\frac{200}{1000}+\frac{40}{1000}+\frac{6}{1000}\\
&=\frac{246}{1000}=0.246.
\end{aligned}
\]
The value is \(0.246\), choice \(\mathrm{D}\).

